{"id": "EUVD-2026-103976", "enisaUuid": "c3471d12-2f4c-3b70-b709-9d7f490de57f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: block2mtd: Fix divide error when erase_size is zero\n\nThe erase size is parsed from the \"block2mtd\" module parameter and can\nbe set to zero. add_device() then evaluates\n\n        if (size % erase_size)\n\nwith a zero divisor, which triggers a divide error:\n\ndivide error: 0000 [#1] PREEMPT SMP PTI\nRIP: 0010:add_device drivers/mtd/devices/block2mtd.c:296 [inline]\nRIP: 0010:block2mtd_setup2+0x592/0xda0 drivers/mtd/devices/block2mtd.c:459\nCall Trace:\nblock2mtd_setup+0x27/0xe0 drivers/mtd/devices/block2mtd.c:476\nparam_attr_store+0x214/0x310 kernel/params.c:589\nmodule_attr_store+0x65/0x90 kernel/params.c:904\nkernfs_fop_write_iter+0x3a4/0x540 fs/kernfs/file.c:345\n...\n\nReject a zero erase size before performing the modulo operation so the\nexisting \"erasesize must be a divisor of device size\" error path\nreports the invalid argument and frees the device.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bff83b723e93acc788bd690dc4bc1f6f4356c35b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/826170a49ca1315af6b293a02200585b1e2186d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a991c28066e7ba4da7450bb04478849f7ac6a14a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21d0f05989bf0d5cef57b467a7fa4feefbd7236a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5965c4221165045e19736794ca5f48ae3d67142"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9h6m-c947-v865", "CVE-2026-98722"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00849512-9df4-363c-85e3-d9fd65dcc752", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea6d833a3fddcd1d60414d48f34c7f4fbe88608f <b5965c4221165045e19736794ca5f48ae3d67142"}, {"id": "1cc5a0e4-dfe8-3ef4-87f7-bc33a64deb49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4434e0d6-ffeb-37c8-8633-33f7f341a428", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea6d833a3fddcd1d60414d48f34c7f4fbe88608f <826170a49ca1315af6b293a02200585b1e2186d9"}, {"id": "70a03e3a-2c4c-3140-98f6-bcaceb811201", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "7268b529-0812-3030-8002-3e0fbcd55453", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea6d833a3fddcd1d60414d48f34c7f4fbe88608f <21d0f05989bf0d5cef57b467a7fa4feefbd7236a"}, {"id": "73e80abf-9938-3420-aa23-ae38f2fd1e48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea6d833a3fddcd1d60414d48f34c7f4fbe88608f <bff83b723e93acc788bd690dc4bc1f6f4356c35b"}, {"id": "809772c2-4310-3637-b09e-ac54e548d759", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ea6d833a3fddcd1d60414d48f34c7f4fbe88608f <a991c28066e7ba4da7450bb04478849f7ac6a14a"}, {"id": "8853df06-3d56-37dc-a3b1-7f66fa556419", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "98fd6e5d-5b68-32c4-ad8c-6bb448726a9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b58f4b98-09cf-3164-9046-0d5755e28087", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "d048ee7d-c836-3142-95c3-140f9ae1cdfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.15"}, {"id": "ec9a2413-aba5-3554-8253-7db71485dfc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7f407f9b-d1e0-3a4b-a64c-44a40a9fd6ee", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}